    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0007:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0007",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "Signal if this is a TLS fallback attempt.",
      "normalizedSource": "Signal if this is a TLS fallback attempt.",
      "sourceHash": "72b58d56a0cd3b8174440ede7e5cd14a54a5f7a27ba9bcea8c9a8110bf9e4826",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "```None\n A fallback attempt is one following a previously failed TLS connection\n due to version or parameter incompatibility, e.g., when speaking to a server\n that does not support a client-offered ciphersuite.\n\n Clients MUST NOT enable fallback for fresh connections.\n```",
      "documentTitle": "secprotocoloptionssettlsisfallbackattempt(::)",
      "framework": "Security",
